    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d690">

                <pb facs="1256" n="1132" xml:id="pg1132"/>

                <head>No. 686.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Blaine to Mr. Fish.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-04-07"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 7,
                        1881</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 205.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 371, in which you inclose an extract from the Berne newspaper Der Bund,
                    respecting the action of the commune of Böttstein, Switzerland, in sending to
                    America an imbecile young woman, name not given, who had hitherto been supported
                    by that commune; and to approve your communication of the facts to the collector
                    of the port of New York, whither, it was understood, she had been sent.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JAMES G. BLAINE.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
